  "findings": [
    "All three correlated drops occur inside both same-host capture windows and have native VFP context.",
    "The matching newly created inbound DR flows retain VXLAN with EncapHeaderAction=Ignore; immediate successful neighbors use Pop on the same DR ports.",
    "Other recorded creation fields match between each failure and both controls, apart from ephemeral port, flow identity and encapsulation transformation.",
    "Protocol 252 records carry encapsulation selectors; raw destination selector 4096 must not be byte-swapped into transport port 16.",
    "Combined Path/ProviderName/Id hashtable queries missed known ETL events on both builds. XPath queries recovered them; original empty outputs are retained as failed-query evidence.",
    "Independent checking found 29 early records in one original XPath slice. The current exporter applies exact UTC bounds after native selection; six native positive, limited and empty exports passed independent XML validation."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Flow tuple/time correlation is context, not an independent packet identity or explanation for the classifier decision.",
    "The earliest retained VFP data events follow capture start; the 64 MiB circular trace may overwrite records. These three contexts were explicitly recovered; completeness of all VFP events is not established.",
    "Packet Monitor reported no events lost, but VFP event loss was not independently audited.",
    "Six failures span complete sampler lifetimes: three have correlated native drops, two other failures occurred during capture without a correlated drop, and one occurred after capture.",
    "No forwarding setting, driver, CNI or image was changed; no mitigation or release is qualified.",
    "Original context slices preserve native XPath selection, including its coarse lower-bound behavior. The selected comparison records are within their requested windows; the corrected exporter is validated separately on retained copies."
  ],
